{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is which modality is most informative for this task. config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) provides the cleanest single-variable comparison: same profile setting (single), same simplicity level (no aggregation/fusion), differing only in modality and encoder. This directly answers whether image features are competitive with or superior to RNA features, which is the foundational design decision that will determine whether to invest the remaining 8 experiments in RNA improvements, image improvements, or multimodal fusion. ResNet50 is also the image encoder used in the multimodal configs, so this result will inform multimodal expectations. Testing this early avoids wasting budget on multimodal or multiprofile variants before knowing which single modality carries signal."
}

